### 9.4 AI Resume Assistant (AI)

Task-based assistant (not a free-form chatbot) available (a) as ✨ buttons next to fields in the builder and (b) on the dedicated Assistant page.

| ID | Feature | Input | Output |
|---|---|---|---|
| AI-01 | Generate summary | personal headline, skills, education, up to 3 experience/project titles | 2–3 summary options (30–80 words) |
| AI-02 | Improve bullet points | 1–10 bullets | Improved version per bullet + reason |
| AI-03 | Rewrite project description | project name, tech stack, current description | Professional rewrite as 2–4 bullets |
| AI-04 | Suggest skills | role headline/target role + existing skills | Up to 15 relevant skills **not already listed**, flagged "add only if you have them" |
| AI-05 | Convert description → achievement bullets | free-text description | 2–4 achievement-oriented bullets with `[add metric]` placeholders instead of invented numbers |
| AI-06 | Grammar & clarity | any text field | Corrected text + list of changes |
| AI-07 | Action-verb suggestions | a bullet | Stronger verb alternatives (deterministic dictionary; works without LLM) |
| AI-08 | Tailor to job description | job description + selected section/bullets | Rewording suggestions emphasising matching *truthful* content + list of JD keywords the user may add if true |

Rules:
- AI-R1: **Suggestions are never written into the resume automatically.** They appear in a visually distinct "AI suggestion" card (sparkle badge, dashed border) with **Accept / Edit then accept / Reject**. Only accepted text becomes resume content.
- AI-R2: The AI must never invent employers, titles, dates, degrees, certifications, awards, or numeric results. Missing metrics are shown as `[add metric]`.
- AI-R3: **Fact guard:** any number, percentage, currency amount, or technology/proper noun in a suggestion that does not appear in the user-supplied source text triggers a visible warning "Contains details not in your original text — verify before accepting."
- AI-R4: Graceful fallback: if the LLM is unavailable/times out/over quota, the API returns a rule-based result with `meta.fallback = true` and the UI shows "AI is unavailable — showing rule-based suggestions."
- AI-R5: API keys exist only in server environment variables.
- AI-R6: First use requires one-time consent ("Selected resume text is sent to a third-party AI provider; contact details are never sent"). Stored as `aiConsentAcceptedAt`.
- AI-R7: Per-user quota: 30 AI requests/day and 10/min (configurable).
- AI-R8: Mock mode (`AI_PROVIDER=mock`) returns deterministic canned outputs for local dev and tests.

**Acceptance criteria**
- AC-AI-1: With `AI_PROVIDER=mock`, every feature returns a valid, schema-conformant result.
- AC-AI-2: With an invalid API key, the endpoint still returns 200 with `meta.fallback=true` (no 500, no key leakage in response or logs).
- AC-AI-3: Input "Built a website for college fest" never yields an output containing an unprovided number such as "10,000 users" without a fact-guard warning.
- AC-AI-4: Rejecting a suggestion leaves the resume unchanged (verified by revision number not incrementing).
- AC-AI-5: Contact details (email, phone, URLs) never appear in the prompt sent to the provider (unit test on prompt builders).

### 9.5 ATS Resume Analyzer (ATS)

A **deterministic, rule-based** engine (no LLM needed for scoring; LLM only enriches suggestions optionally).

| ID | Requirement | P |
|---|---|---|
| ATS-01 | Overall score 0–100 plus sub-scores (0–100 each): Keyword match, Skills match, Formatting, Content quality, Completeness. Weighting in §11.3. | M |
| ATS-02 | Works **without** a job description (keyword and skills sub-scores show "N/A — add a job description"; weights redistributed). | M |
| ATS-03 | Section detection: lists which standard sections are present/missing/empty. | M |
| ATS-04 | Formatting checks F1–F10 and content checks C1–C9 (§11.3), each with pass/fail, explanation and fix. | M |
| ATS-05 | Missing-information detection (e.g., no phone, no skills, no projects for a fresher). | M |
| ATS-06 | Action-verb suggestions for bullets not starting with a strong verb. | M |
| ATS-07 | Prioritised recommendation list (high/medium/low) with deep links to the exact section/entry in the builder. | M |
| ATS-08 | Persist reports (last 10 per resume) and show score history. | S |
| ATS-09 | **Disclaimer always visible:** "This is an estimated heuristic score to help you improve your resume. It is not a guarantee of passing any company's ATS." | M |

**Acceptance criteria**
- AC-ATS-1: Same resume + same JD yields identical scores on repeated runs.
- AC-ATS-2: An empty resume scores < 20; the sample resume without JD scores ≥ 70; fixture resumes land in their expected bands (±5).
- AC-ATS-3: Report renders in ≤ 2 s (API p95 ≤ 500 ms).
- AC-ATS-4: Every recommendation links to a section that exists in the resume.

