## 11. Calculations

### 11.1 Dates
Stored as `"YYYY-MM"` or `""`; `current: true` means "Present". Display format set by template (e.g., "Jun 2025").

### 11.2 Completion percentage (0–100)
Contact (name, email, phone, location present) **15** · Headline or summary **10** · Education ≥1 entry **15** · Skills ≥1 group with items **15** · Experience or Internships ≥1 entry **15** · Projects ≥1 entry **15** · ≥1 link (LinkedIn/GitHub/portfolio) **5** · ≥1 extra entry in Certifications/Achievements/Extracurricular/Languages/Custom **10**. Implemented once in `shared/` and reused by client and server.

### 11.3 ATS scoring (authoritative; ARCHITECTURE.md implements it)
- **With JD:** Keyword 30% · Skills 15% · Formatting 20% · Content 20% · Completeness 15%.
- **Without JD:** Formatting 30% · Content 40% · Completeness 30%.
- **Formatting checks (F1–F10):** F1 email+phone present and valid · F2 standard section headings · F3 template `atsSafe` · F4 estimated ≤ 2 pages (≤ 1 page expected when < 3 years' experience) · F5 dates present & consistent · F6 reverse-chronological order · F7 no visible empty sections · F8 no emoji/special glyphs, no all-caps paragraphs · F9 2–6 bullets per experience/project entry · F10 valid URLs.
- **Content checks (C1–C9):** C1 ≥ 80% bullets start with a strong action verb · C2 ≥ 30% bullets quantified · C3 bullet length 8–28 words · C4 no weak phrases ("responsible for", "worked on", "helped with", "duties included") · C5 no first-person pronouns · C6 summary 30–80 words · C7 no verb used to start > 2 bullets · C8 8–25 skills listed · C9 no clichés ("hard-working", "team player", "go-getter", "results-oriented").
- Keyword match % = importance-weighted share of JD keywords found in resume text (alias- and stem-aware). Skills match % = share of dictionary skills in the JD found in the resume.

