## 12. Non-Functional Requirements

| Area | Requirement |
|---|---|
| Security | See §19. OWASP Top-10 aware; no secrets in code or repo. |
| Validation | Zod schemas validate **every** request body/query/params; unknown keys rejected. |
| AuthZ | Every resume/analysis query filters by `userId`. |
| Error handling | Uniform error envelope with `code`, `message`, `requestId`; no stack traces in production responses. |
| Persistence | MongoDB; autosave + revision counter; no data in localStorage except UI preferences. |
| Performance | CRUD API p95 ≤ 300 ms (excluding AI/PDF); ATS ≤ 500 ms; PDF ≤ 10 s; route-level code splitting; landing JS ≤ 250 KB gzipped. |
| Responsive | Works at 360 px, 768 px, 1280 px+ widths. Builder: 3-pane desktop, tabbed Edit/Preview on tablet/mobile. |
| Accessibility | WCAG 2.1 AA target: keyboard operable (including reorder), visible focus, labels on inputs, `aria-live` for save status and toasts, contrast ≥ 4.5:1, reduced-motion respected. |
| Maintainability | TypeScript strict; ESLint + Prettier; shared types/schemas in `shared/`; feature-based folders. |
| Reusability | Shared UI primitives; one template-primitives kit reused by all four templates. |
| Config | All config via validated environment variables (`.env.example` committed, `.env` ignored). |
| Logging | Structured JSON logs (pino) with request IDs; **never log passwords, tokens, API keys, resume content, or JD text**. |
| Testing | Unit + integration + one E2E happy path; coverage targets in AGENT.md. |
| Privacy | Contact details never sent to the LLM; user can export and delete all data. |

## 13. Complete Feature Descriptions — Key UX Behaviour

- **Builder layout (≥1024 px):** left rail = section list (drag handle, eye toggle, "+ Add section"); center = active section editor; right = live A4 preview with zoom (fit/100%) and page-break guides. Header: inline-editable title, save status, completion ring, Template, ✨ Assistant, ATS, Download PDF.
- **Builder layout (<1024 px):** segmented control **Edit | Preview**; section list becomes a horizontal chip scroller / drawer.
- **Entry cards:** collapsible, with drag handle, duplicate, delete (undo toast for 6 s).
- **✨ buttons:** open a popover with suggestion cards; accepting patches the field and triggers autosave.
- **ATS page:** left = JD textarea (optional) + "Analyze"; right = score gauge, sub-score bars, collapsible check lists, prioritised recommendations with "Go fix" links; history sparkline.
- **JD Matcher page:** two-column: JD input → results (matched/missing chips, per-section suggestions, "Create tailored copy").
- **Assistant page:** feature tabs (Summary, Bullets, Project, Skills, Achievements, Grammar, Verbs, Tailor); choose resume + target field or paste text; results as suggestion cards with Accept (writes to chosen field) / Copy / Reject.

