## 17. UI/UX Requirements

- Style references: Linear, Notion, Vercel — clean, minimal, generous whitespace.
- Tokens: background `#FFFFFF`/`#F9FAFB`, borders `#E5E7EB`, text `#111827`/`#4B5563`, primary indigo `#4F46E5` (hover `#4338CA`), success `#059669`, warning `#D97706`, danger `#DC2626`. Radius: cards 12 px, inputs/buttons 8 px. Shadows: `shadow-sm` default, `shadow-md` on hover/popovers. Transitions 150–200 ms.
- Typography (app UI): Inter, 14/16 px base, clear heading scale.
- States required for every async view: loading skeleton, empty, error with retry, success toast.
- AI content is always visually marked (sparkle badge + dashed indigo border).
- Landing page: hero (headline, subcopy, 2 CTAs, product screenshot-like **live** template preview), feature highlights (6), how it works (3 steps), template previews (4, real components with sample data), CTA band, footer.
- Dark mode: not required (out of scope).

## 18. Database-Related Requirements

Collections: `users`, `resumes`, `refreshTokens`, `analyses`, `aiUsage`. Embedded sections inside `resumes`; indexes on `{userId, updatedAt}`; unique index on `users.email` (lowercased); TTL indexes on `refreshTokens.expiresAt` and `aiUsage.createdAt` (30 days). Details in ARCHITECTURE.md §15–16.

## 19. API & Security Requirements

**API:** REST under `/api/v1`, JSON, uniform envelope `{ data }` / `{ error }`, proper status codes, pagination on lists, idempotent PATCH with `baseRevision`. Complete table in ARCHITECTURE.md §14.

**Security:** bcrypt; JWT with strict algorithm; refresh-token rotation with reuse detection; httpOnly cookies; Helmet headers; CORS allow-list; rate limits (auth, AI, global); body size limit 1 MB; Zod validation; NoSQL-injection-safe (typed schemas, no raw query objects from clients); output rendered as text in React (no `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`); PDF renderer restricted to the app's own origin with single-use, 60-second print tokens; prompt-injection mitigations for JD/resume text; dependency audit in CI; secrets only via environment.

