## 23. Constraints & Assumptions (engineering decisions made to remove ambiguity)

1. **Free-tier friendly:** MongoDB Atlas M0, free LLM tier (Google Gemini API via AI Studio by default), free hosting tiers. No paid dependency is required.
2. **LLM provider is pluggable** (`gemini`, `openai`-compatible, `mock`); model names come from env vars because they change over time.
3. **ATS "score" is a heuristic.** No real company ATS is emulated; the UI says so.
4. **PDF engine = headless Chromium (Puppeteer)** rendering the real React templates → fidelity + selectable text. Browser-print fallback exists because Chromium hosting on free tiers can be constrained.
5. **Single-origin deployment illusion:** the frontend host proxies `/api/*` to the backend so cookies are first-party and CORS is unnecessary in production.
6. **No email infrastructure in MVP** → no verification/forgot-password; users can change password while signed in.
7. **Plain-text bullets** (no rich text) for ATS safety and simpler PDF.
8. **Sample resume is real persisted data** (created by the backend at registration), not frontend mock data.
9. **English-language resumes** only; Latin-script fonts bundled.
10. Resume content is stored as structured JSON, not as generated HTML.
11. Single deployed backend instance (in-memory rate-limit stores acceptable).
12. Desktop-class Chromium available in the deployment environment (Docker image) for PDF.

